<h2 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="upgrade-process" aria-labelledby="_R_v9deehkd74t9_"><a href="#upgrade-process" class="anchor-link" aria-label="Navigate to header: Upgrade process"></a><span id="_R_v9deehkd74t9_" class="cursor-pointer">Upgrade process</span></h2>
<span data-as="p">Network upgrades follow this general process in which the features included in
the upgrade are put into a release version cut from the <code>develop</code> branch and
then the software is deployed on production networks.</span>
<div role="note" aria-label="Info" class="callout my-4 px-5 py-4 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl flex gap-3 border border-neutral-200 bg-neutral-50 dark:border-neutral-700 dark:bg-white/10" data-callout-type="info"><div class="mt-0.5 w-4" data-component-part="callout-icon"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="18" stroke-width="1.5" class="flex-none size-5 text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-300"><use href="#mi-mint-1-CalloutInfo"></use></svg></div><div class="text-sm prose dark:prose-invert min-w-0 w-full [&amp;_kbd]:bg-background-light dark:[&amp;_kbd]:bg-background-dark [&amp;_code]:text-current! [&amp;_kbd]:text-current! [&amp;_a]:text-current! [&amp;_a]:border-current [&amp;_strong]:text-current! text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-300" data-component-part="callout-content"><span data-as="p">“Baking” on a network means the node software has been deployed and is live.
Engineers take this time to observe the behavior of the software on
production networks.</span></div></div>
